1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,905
Step one. Install the tools needed.

2
00:00:02,025 --> 00:00:05,518
The two most important tools needed are Claude Code and Hyperframes.

3
00:00:05,638 --> 00:00:08,178
Others are FFmpeg and Node.js version 22.

4
00:00:08,298 --> 00:00:10,204
Here is what each tool contributes.

5
00:00:10,324 --> 00:00:13,816
The Claude Code is the AI assistant working inside our project.

6
00:00:13,936 --> 00:00:17,429
We give it instructions, and it creates and edits the files.

7
00:00:17,549 --> 00:00:20,725
In this case, we make use of its desktop app.

8
00:00:20,845 --> 00:00:23,067
The Hyperframes is an open-source tool

9
00:00:23,187 --> 00:00:25,728
that provides the framework for turning HTML, CSS,

10
00:00:25,848 --> 00:00:27,753
media, and animations into a video.

11
00:00:27,873 --> 00:00:30,731
The Node.js 22 is an open-source app

12
00:00:30,851 --> 00:00:33,708
that installs the framework packages and run project tools.

13
00:00:33,828 --> 00:00:35,099
And the last, FFmpeg.

14
00:00:35,219 --> 00:00:38,712
It's also an open-source app that turns rendered frames

15
00:00:38,832 --> 00:00:40,419
into an export MP4 file.

16
00:00:40,539 --> 00:00:43,397
Simply download and install them into your computer system.

17
00:00:43,517 --> 00:00:46,375
The download links are in the video description below.

18
00:00:46,495 --> 00:00:48,400
Let's move to step two.
